The maximal possible rank of the matrix representing the flag of Tonga is 4. An image of the flag is partitioned into four distinct horizontal row profiles: the red field, the white canton margin, the vertical cross arm, and the horizontal cross arm. Selecting these four physical row types alongside four corresponding vertical column zones yields an explicit 4x4 submatrix with determinant $-a(b-a)^3$, which is non-zero for any non-trivial pixel values $a \neq 0$ and $b \neq a$. Because the full row space is spanned by at most four distinct vectors and contains an invertible order-4 minor, the rank is unconditionally 4.
}

